hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27911","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Muammal narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Ata narrated to us, from Habibah bint Abi Tajrah, she said: We entered the house of Abu Husayn among women of Quraysh, while the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was circumambulating between al-Safa and al-Marwah. She said: And he was running, his waist-wrapper turning about him from the vehemence of the running, and he was saying to his companions: Run, for Allah has prescribed running upon you."
"27912","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Muammal narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Habibah bint Abi Tajrah, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, circumambulating between al-Safa and al-Marwah, with the people before him and he behind them, and he was running until I saw his knees from the vehemence of the running, his waist-wrapper turning about him, and he was saying: Run, for Allah has prescribed running upon you."
